{"name":"Standing Waters","hex":"#005599","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"standing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of stand"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Erect, not cut down.","Performed from an erect position."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/standing"},{"term":"waters","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of water","Amniotic fluid ."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of water"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waters"}],"entries":[{"title":"Standing","blocks":[{"text":"Standing, also referred to as orthostasis, is a position in which the body is held in an upright (orthostatic) position and supported only by the feet. Although seemingly static, the body rocks slightly back and forth from the ankle in the sagittal plane, which bisects the body into right and left sides. The sway of quiet standing is often likened to the motion of an inverted pendulum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Yerevan%2C_Armenian_girls_posing_in_photo_shoot%2C_Acting%2C_Posture%2C_Body_language%2C_Armenia.jpg/330px-Yerevan%2C_Armenian_girls_posing_in_photo_shoot%2C_Acting%2C_Posture%2C_Body_language%2C_Armenia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standing","wikidata":"Q1986098"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Yerevan%2C_Armenian_girls_posing_in_photo_shoot%2C_Acting%2C_Posture%2C_Body_language%2C_Armenia.jpg/500px-Yerevan%2C_Armenian_girls_posing_in_photo_shoot%2C_Acting%2C_Posture%2C_Body_language%2C_Armenia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Yerevan%2C_Armenian_girls_posing_in_photo_shoot%2C_Acting%2C_Posture%2C_Body_language%2C_Armenia.jpg/1280px-Yerevan%2C_Armeni